> gain energy potion

Not critical for a while, I usually alchemize just before doing the
ascension run (used to be after clearing Gehennom, which I think is a
good plan for you--I'll usually do it in one go now).

> charging scrolls

They're nice to find before the castle wand but worth the wish if not
found.

> cancellation wands

Watch that BoH.  Cancellation isn't critical, but can help in a few
situations (uncursing/eliminating negative enchantments on stuff, and
makes blanking potions/scrolls a bit less tedious but isn't needed
there).

> slow digestion

Pretty useless by now--you're at the stage where if you lack tinning,
the hard part is getting unsatiated quickly enough.

> free action

Nice but not critical (gelcubes and !paralysis are the only things it
really helps against, and the former you can avoid with ranged
attacks).  It can occasionally stop a frustrating death.

> conflict, teleport control

These are _huge_.  Conflict is stupidly powerful, and telecontrol
makes for a much less tedious game (and allows you to start eating
tengu for the intrinsic).

> poly control
Meh.  I've almost never used it, except in funky situations (once I
had a low-level character #poly into a black dragon to dispose of a
baddy on a bones level, that was fun).

> The only amulets I have seen are ESP and reflect

Those are 2 of the best, life saving is probably a good idea for you
and magical breathing sometimes handy.  The others are pretty much
worthless unless you're doing oddball tactics (you already have poison
resistance I presume).

> gloves of power (I'm using +5dex anyway)

You've got the best gloves in the game.  Power is nice really early
for weak classes but they kill spellcasting chances (which you're
already struggling with) and don't give you any real benefit over 18/
** strength (and not a huge benefit over str close to that).  You can
take them off to cast as long as you remember to put them back on, but
beware that you will forget to put them on the next time you decide to
pick up a c corpse.

> Speed and jumping boots.

Both are nice, jumping are a bit better once you figure them out but
speed are better out of the box for first-timers.

