The castle is a breeze with patience and an instrument, or pretty easy
with levitation and conflict.  The first few levels of Gehennom aren't
bad and you'll get a lot of loot in the Valley.  Just keep the Eye's
airlift-to-safety feature in mind (and know its limitations, e.g. with
respect to L and a few other things that will follow along with you).

> At this point do I wish for SDSM with the castle wand or just wait to
> farm it off a dragon? I have reflection from an amulet, resistance
> covered 3x over and MC3 from robe/oilskin.

Do you have _any_ DSM?  If not I'd make some from a Castle dragon just
for the AC.  I wouldn't burn a wish on it, and certainly not unless
you find a "oLifeSaving.  Though ESP is a nice early-warning system.
Kind of your call, I guess.

It's not uncommon if you know ?genocide already to wish for a cursed
marker and reverse-geno silver dragons rather than wishing for the
DSM.  If you have undead turning that helps.  The cursed marker can
also get you wraiths/nurses and a couple cursed gold detection, then
be blessed and used for other stuff.

But it doesn't _guarantee_ scales.  In your case where you don't
absolutely need reflection, it might be worth considering.

